Today I had my first ascension, and this marks my first ascension
post.  I didn't keep an actual log throughout the course of the game,
but I can certainly sum up the main points :D

To start with, money was never a problem... though I really never
bought much from shops.  As I made my way to minetown, I encountered
the bones of an unfortunate samurai who graciously donated two
spellbooks and gray dragon scale mail.  At this point I turned tail
and completed Sokoban, gaining a Bag of Holding.  I returned to the
mines and...  Minetown was exceptionally uneventful, the only good
find was a magic lamp... the temple was cross-aligned.  This lamp in
minetown was blessed, and thus I received my first wish (cloak of
displacement).  I had previously found an uncursed magic lamp, which I
decided to keep as an ever-burning lamp, named Nightbane.  There was
an altar on floor 18 (and another co-aligned altar a few floors
higher, but it was rather inconvenient).  The quest portal was here,
and I have been gifted with several wraiths and potions of gain level
by now.  I enter the quest at level 17, and leave at 22 with the
Longbow of Diana.  Scorpius was an overall pushover :)  I emptied all
my wands of create monster and scrolls of create monster, and received
Werebane, which I used for quite a while.

At floor 22 I found a large leprechaun hall, and a second hall on
floor 23.  I stashed 53,000 gold there, to return for later.  By this
point, I had a decent assortment of rings and wands, and a nice amulet
of magical breathing.  I took the aquatic route through Medusa's Swamp
and stoned her with the ol' mirror trick.  Perseus had a Shield of
Reflection, which I gladly relieved him of.

Castle was on floor 28, snuck around the back with no problems and
grabbed the wand of wishing.  Not sure what all I wished for, but the
Master Key of Thievery took two tries to succeed (there were at least
4 artifacts by now... )

Trudging through Gehennom was slow, and I mapped the entire place
manually (with my Nightbane, of course).  As I cross Juiblex's swamp
(wand of digging made an easy kill) along the bottom I lose most of my
scrolls and spellbooks without realising it...  at this point I had a
spellbook of Identify which I have been making a lot of use of.  No
wands of polymorph yet, and no wands of death or wishing.  I note that
I have found (and left) my THIRD amulet of ESP (useless, as the
Longbow of Diana grants it)... I have a large collection of rings and
wands now, my ascension kit is nearly complete, except...

No magic markers and no scrolls of enchant armor make me a very easy
to hit boy.  I dump my slow digging implements and wands of striking
at some early point in gehenom, and at this point I have two bags of
holding, boots of speed, and am burdened.

In orcus town, I make quick work of orcus (cockatrice corpse) and find
I have no way to open him up.  That was a sad day.  I find and clear
rodney's tower (except the topmost floor) quickly, and head down to
floor 51, where I find the vibrating square for the first time ever.
I mark it with an iron chain (I love those things).  At this point I'm
burdened, very fast, MC2, have reflection and magic resistance, half
physical damage... and -2 AC.  Everyone in the IRC thinks I'm crazy.

At some point while I was in Gehennom, on the #nethack channel (you
guys are awesome) someone suggested I stone and bring Izchak, as a
conduct.  I was made very happy by this idea, and after some
wiztesting and calculations, I decided it was definitely possible to
do (without abusing bugs), and that I would try my best to do it.

I head all the way back up, to hit up minetown for candles and to
retrieve Izchak.  I polymorph into a nymph (I have the polymorph and
poly control rings already, of course) and relieve him of his items,
and poly into a leprechaun to relieve his gold as well.  A cockatrice
corpse to stun him, and into the bag he goes.  I decided I need a
spellbook of stone to flesh, to keep things good once we get to the
demigod bar, so I spend the next day using up all my wands of create
monster (again) and casting the create monster spell.  Largely
uneventful, and no spellbook.  I get crowned at this point, but I
don't get anything out of it except stormbringer (already have all the
resistances at this point, it was kinda weird feeling....)  I throw
werebane into the bag at this point.

Back up to floor one.  I find a shop along the way and identify the
wands inside, and find a wand of polymorph!  Back to floor 18, where I
start polymorphing all my spellbooks to (after a couple of hours) find
a spellbook of stone to flesh!  Back on floor one, I put the book and
a candy bar in the Izchakmobile, and head down, ready for the
ascension run.  The blessed Izchakmobile will take up 55% of my
inventory space... this is going to be *hard*, seeing as how I'm a
packrat, and am still burdened with just my normal gear.

I easily grab the book of the dead, levelport to the vibrating square,
use my Nightbane to get a wish, and wish for 7 candles (minetown only
supplied 5, so I needed 2 more), and head inside to get the amulet.  I
have very little equipment that can burn, and it is already burnt (so
I lost maybe 2 AC), so I just walk around the temple to find my way
in.  Right before the run, used my last wish to get a magic marker,
with which I made several scrolls of enchant armor...  combined with
my AC from donating to the minetown priest during my second visit, and
from 3 more AC granted by my god, I have about -26 AC.

Running back up, it's making me tense a bit, seeing as I've never done
it before, and I'm waiting for Rodney to appear.  On floor 40,
Yeenoghu is summoned, somehow (not sure how), and I'm stuck having to
manually cross the map from the right to the left side.  About halfway
across the top, in the thin hallway (he's not hurting me much, but it
is terribly annoying)  he starts summoning more demons, and progress
comes to a *very* slow pace.  Wand of teleport to the rescue!  I may
not be able to teleport, but they sure can...  At the other side, I am
met by a cockatrice and a demon with a wand of death.  I grab the
(now) dead cockatrice and make short work of Yeenoghu (that was a
happy moment, that guy was driving me nuts), and I stone the wand of
death guy, too.  Now, another demon, behind the wand of death guy, has
a wand of striking.  He politely breaks Yeenoghu and the wand of death
demon, I retrieve the wand (it is my second), and stone the striker.
Running back up is largely uneventful past this point... still waiting
for Rodney to show up...

Back on floor 2 or 3, Rodney appears.  Wand of death'd him, continued
up.  Stopped and picked up the Izchakmobile, dropped a *lot* of stuff,
am still burdened.  Decided I'd wait until the end of the plane of
earth, and then I'd dump all my wands of digging, and maybe then I
would be unburdened.  I can only carry 900 weight naturally, so I
levitate through the plane of earth, quickly locating the portal.
Couldn't dump enough to get unburdened... oh well... I'll just wait
and dump before entering Astral...

Plane of Air took a while.  Wasn't much of a problem, but it went a
lot faster once I put on the blindfold.  The amulet didn't help me out
much, so I randomly walked into the portal and landed in the plane of
fire.  Confusion + scroll of gold detection trick, levitated across,
again uneventful, and faster than air, now that I'm wearing the
blindfold.

I thought the plane of water was absolutely awesome.  Anyways, at the
portal in the plane of water, I dump & dump & dump.  I quaff most of
my potions of full healing, drop most of my food (I'll enter astral
with only 4 K-rations), keep only wands of death and teleport, helm of
reverse alignment...  Somehow I manage to become unburdened.  I'll be
using the jump & wand of teleport method to navigate as fast as I can
on astral (casting jump, I'm wearing speed boots).  I only bring... 3
holy waters, blessed scroll of genocide, and a blessed remove curse.
(And my other main equipment), I have to drop my Stormbringer and
Werebane now, and my bag of gems (sad day...), and I am no longer
burdened.  I will use a ring of free action and a ring of conflict on
astral.  I use up the last of my marker writing scrolls of enchant
armor, and I have -32 AC.  I ditch the shield of reflection and rely
on the Bow of Diana for reflection, and as my main weapon.  I only
bring 35 arrows (maybe less).

Atral was pretty annoying... the priests only summoned ants when the
Riders were right next to me... and the Angels absolutely *loved*
standing in the doorways.  I start by heading right, where Death is
waiting.  I glance inside and notice a priest of a different
alignment, so I leave (it was lawful, but I thought it was neutral).
Headed back, and pestilence is at the middle altar, where the real
neutral altar is.  This is sad, so I decide I'll head back and check
what the altar on the right is - if it is lawful or chaotic, I can
still ascend, and it has to be one of the two, so I'll ascend this
time!  I use the last of my holy water uncursing my ring of conflict,
to make navigation easier...  and reach the lawful altar.  My elvish
helm is cursed.  I have no way to uncurse it now.  So, I ditch the
useless helmet and pull out my last wand of death and my fourth to
last wand of teleport... head to the far left altar, where I meet two
different aligned high priests.  *now* I was confused, and I figured
it was that I was having too much fun with the wand of teleport :D  I
stand on the altar, and notice that some creatures don't attack me, I
have finally reached the high altar!  I check to make sure I still
have Izchak, the high priest gives me 2 bits, and I offer the
Amulet :)

